{"module":"schools","voice":"female","duration":177.8,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Schools: separate, unequal and still divided","start":0.0,"end":4.48,"words":[[0.05,0.67],[1.03,1.75],[2.11,2.83],[2.83,3.14],[3.14,3.55],[3.55,4.37]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Education has always been both a target and a path to freedom.","start":5.28,"end":9.12,"words":[[5.33,6.01],[6.01,6.21],[6.21,6.62],[6.62,6.82],[6.82,7.1],[7.1,7.23],[7.23,7.57],[7.57,7.77],[7.77,7.91],[7.91,8.11],[8.11,8.25],[8.25,8.72]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Enslaved people were forbidden to read; their children built thousands of schools.","start":9.47,"end":14.65,"words":[[9.52,10.12],[10.12,10.49],[10.49,10.63],[10.63,11.15],[11.15,11.3],[11.3,11.59],[11.85,12.07],[12.07,12.67],[12.67,12.96],[12.96,13.55],[13.55,13.7],[13.7,14.14]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Forbidden to read, determined to learn","start":15.0,"end":17.35,"words":[[15.0,15.53],[15.53,15.68],[15.68,15.98],[16.25,16.85],[16.85,17.0],[17.0,17.23]]},{"el":"s0","text":"After Nat Turner's rebellion, Southern states tightened laws against teaching enslaved people to read.","start":18.05,"end":23.7,"words":[[18.1,18.37],[18.37,18.57],[18.57,18.91],[18.91,19.52],[19.76,20.09],[20.09,20.5],[20.5,20.97],[20.97,21.18],[21.18,21.58],[21.58,21.99],[21.99,22.53],[22.53,22.87],[22.87,23.01],[23.01,23.28]]},{"el":"s0","text":"After emancipation, freed people built and funded schools themselves, with help from the Freedmen's Bureau.","start":24.05,"end":31.19,"words":[[24.11,24.41],[24.41,25.37],[25.63,25.92],[25.92,26.29],[26.29,26.59],[26.59,26.81],[26.81,27.25],[27.25,27.62],[27.62,28.29],[28.54,28.77],[28.77,29.06],[29.06,29.36],[29.36,29.5],[29.5,30.1],[30.1,30.69]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Between 1912 and 1932, Black communities, Booker T. Washington and philanthropist Julius Rosenwald built nearly 5,000 “Rosenwald schools” across the South, with Black families raising much of the money.","start":31.54,"end":46.7,"words":[[31.59,32.04],[32.04,32.95],[32.95,33.18],[33.18,34.23],[34.5,34.8],[34.8,35.63],[35.89,36.2],[36.2,36.42],[36.8,37.4],[37.4,37.63],[37.63,38.54],[38.54,39.14],[39.14,39.9],[39.9,40.2],[40.2,40.58],[40.58,41.41],[41.41,42.16],[42.16,42.54],[42.54,42.92],[42.92,43.07],[43.07,43.44],[43.71,43.94],[43.94,44.24],[44.24,44.77],[44.77,45.22],[45.22,45.52],[45.52,45.67],[45.67,45.82],[45.82,46.2]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Brown, and massive resistance","start":47.6,"end":50.22,"words":[[47.66,48.21],[48.53,48.81],[48.81,49.27],[49.27,50.09]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Brown v. Board of Education (1954) ruled segregated schools unconstitutional; a year later the Court ordered desegregation “with all deliberate speed,” which many states treated as never.","start":50.92,"end":63.72,"words":[[50.96,51.33],[51.33,51.55],[51.92,52.15],[52.15,52.3],[52.3,53.04],[53.04,54.08],[54.34,54.64],[54.64,55.46],[55.46,55.83],[55.83,57.1],[57.36,57.51],[57.51,57.73],[57.73,58.1],[58.1,58.25],[58.25,58.48],[58.48,58.77],[58.77,59.74],[59.74,59.96],[59.96,60.11],[60.11,60.78],[60.78,61.16],[61.16,61.45],[61.45,61.75],[61.75,62.2],[62.2,62.64],[62.64,62.79],[62.79,63.17]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The Little Rock Nine needed federal troops in 1957; six-year-old Ruby Bridges needed federal marshals in 1960.","start":64.07,"end":73.49,"words":[[64.12,64.28],[64.28,64.68],[64.68,64.92],[64.92,65.24],[65.24,65.64],[65.64,66.2],[66.2,66.59],[66.59,66.75],[66.75,68.19],[68.47,69.42],[69.42,69.74],[69.74,70.3],[70.3,70.7],[70.7,71.26],[71.26,71.74],[71.74,71.9],[71.9,73.01]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Prince Edward County, Virginia, closed its public schools from 1959 to 1964 rather than integrate, while white students attended private “segregation academies.”","start":73.84,"end":86.74,"words":[[73.84,74.22],[74.22,74.6],[74.6,75.13],[75.4,76.09],[76.35,76.81],[76.81,77.04],[77.04,77.5],[77.5,77.88],[77.88,78.18],[78.18,79.4],[79.4,79.55],[79.55,80.7],[80.7,81.0],[81.0,81.23],[81.23,81.99],[82.26,82.57],[82.57,82.87],[82.87,83.56],[83.56,84.09],[84.09,84.62],[84.62,85.46],[85.46,86.15]]},{"el":"h2","text":"The educators who were pushed out","start":87.64,"end":89.51,"words":[[87.69,87.84],[87.84,88.58],[88.58,88.73],[88.73,88.87],[88.87,89.17],[89.17,89.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"As schools merged, Black schools were usually closed and Black principals and teachers fired or demoted.","start":90.21,"end":96.87,"words":[[90.26,90.41],[90.41,90.78],[90.78,91.23],[91.5,91.8],[91.8,92.17],[92.17,92.32],[92.32,92.85],[92.85,93.3],[93.3,93.53],[93.53,93.83],[93.83,94.58],[94.58,94.81],[94.81,95.26],[95.26,95.63],[95.63,95.71],[95.71,96.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"An estimated 38,000 Black teachers and administrators in 17 Southern and border states lost their jobs between 1954 and 1965.","start":97.22,"end":108.32,"words":[[97.27,97.43],[97.43,98.21],[98.21,99.38],[99.38,99.69],[99.69,100.16],[100.16,100.39],[100.39,101.48],[101.48,101.64],[101.64,102.26],[102.26,102.65],[102.65,102.89],[102.89,103.2],[103.2,103.67],[103.67,103.98],[103.98,104.22],[104.22,104.61],[104.61,105.07],[105.07,106.17],[106.17,106.4],[106.4,107.81]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Research today finds that Black students who have even one Black teacher are more likely to graduate and go to college.","start":108.67,"end":116.05,"words":[[108.72,109.18],[109.18,109.57],[109.57,110.03],[110.03,110.26],[110.26,110.57],[110.57,111.26],[111.26,111.41],[111.41,111.64],[111.64,111.95],[111.95,112.18],[112.18,112.49],[112.49,112.87],[112.87,112.95],[112.95,113.1],[113.1,113.57],[113.57,113.72],[113.72,114.33],[114.33,114.57],[114.57,114.8],[114.8,114.95],[114.95,115.49]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Busing, and the line at the city limits","start":116.95,"end":119.69,"words":[[117.02,117.49],[117.76,117.99],[117.99,118.14],[118.14,118.45],[118.45,118.6],[118.6,118.76],[118.76,119.07],[119.07,119.53]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The Supreme Court upheld busing to desegregate within a district in 1971 (Swann).","start":120.39,"end":126.21,"words":[[120.44,120.59],[120.59,121.01],[121.01,121.23],[121.23,121.66],[121.66,122.02],[122.02,122.16],[122.16,122.95],[122.95,123.3],[123.3,123.45],[123.45,124.02],[124.02,124.16],[124.16,125.38],[125.38,125.73]]},{"el":"s3","text":"But in Milliken v. Bradley (1974) it barred courts from including mostly white suburbs in Detroit's remedy, so families could avoid desegregation by moving across a district line.","start":126.56,"end":138.7,"words":[[126.62,126.83],[126.83,126.98],[126.98,127.47],[127.47,127.69],[128.05,128.47],[128.47,129.61],[129.86,130.0],[130.0,130.22],[130.22,130.5],[130.5,130.79],[130.79,131.36],[131.36,131.86],[131.86,132.14],[132.14,132.57],[132.57,132.71],[132.71,133.28],[133.28,133.78],[134.03,134.25],[134.25,134.74],[134.74,134.96],[134.96,135.31],[135.31,136.24],[136.24,136.45],[136.45,136.81],[136.81,137.17],[137.17,137.31],[137.31,137.88],[137.88,138.24]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Resegregation and funding today","start":139.6,"end":141.93,"words":[[139.66,140.7],[140.7,140.94],[140.94,141.42],[141.42,141.82]]},{"el":"s4","text":"A 2016 federal report (GAO) found the share of schools that are high-poverty and mostly Black or Hispanic grew from 2000 to 2013; researchers debate how much this reflects housing patterns versus policy choices.","start":142.63,"end":157.49,"words":[[142.68,142.83],[142.83,143.84],[143.84,144.39],[144.39,144.78],[144.78,145.01],[145.28,145.67],[145.67,145.83],[145.83,146.06],[146.06,146.22],[146.22,146.61],[146.61,146.84],[146.84,146.92],[146.92,147.62],[147.62,147.85],[147.85,148.4],[148.4,148.71],[148.71,148.79],[148.79,149.41],[149.41,149.64],[149.64,149.96],[149.96,150.66],[150.66,150.81],[150.81,151.75],[152.02,152.64],[152.64,153.11],[153.11,153.34],[153.34,153.65],[153.65,153.89],[153.89,154.51],[154.51,154.98],[154.98,155.44],[155.44,155.83],[155.83,156.3],[156.3,156.92]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Funding gaps are documented: a 2019 EdBuild analysis estimated that districts serving mostly students of color received about $23 billion less a year than mostly white districts serving the same number of students, largely because schools rely on local property taxes.","start":157.84,"end":176.87,"words":[[157.89,158.35],[158.35,158.65],[158.65,158.73],[158.73,159.65],[159.92,160.07],[160.07,161.07],[161.07,161.53],[161.53,162.14],[162.14,162.9],[162.9,163.13],[163.13,163.82],[163.82,164.21],[164.21,164.74],[164.74,165.43],[165.43,165.58],[165.58,165.89],[165.89,166.35],[166.35,166.73],[166.73,167.73],[167.73,168.19],[168.19,168.42],[168.42,168.57],[168.57,168.8],[168.8,169.03],[169.03,169.57],[169.57,169.87],[169.87,170.56],[170.56,170.95],[170.95,171.1],[171.1,171.41],[171.41,171.79],[171.79,171.94],[171.94,172.71],[172.98,173.44],[173.44,173.82],[173.82,174.2],[174.2,174.59],[174.59,174.74],[174.74,175.2],[175.2,175.73],[175.73,176.27]]}]}